  "curriculumPageSha256": "cbcb9fb705d7a5d6d9244e05a9ad881798b8bb793e6f39cd9cad17bfefe52720",
  "curriculum": "UvA’s regular Dutch-language full-time Biology bachelor (RIO 56860) totals 180 EC. The first year builds from cells, genetics, microbes and data to animals, plants, ecology and the sustainability policy project. The second year connects cellular responses, immunity, neurobiology and evolution with quantitative analysis and team research. Year three leaves 30 EC open, then includes 6 EC each for project design and bioinformatics plus the required 18 EC bachelor project. No named comparator specialisation is selected.",
  "progression": "The normal year-one plan contains 60 EC and exceeds the programme study-guidance page’s 42 EC binding-study-advice threshold. The Living Cell supplies the stated background for Cellular Responses. Data collection, R and experimental design precede Quantitative Biology, ecology/evolution team research and Big Data. Research Project Design and Planning prepares students to propose, conduct and report the final supervised individual project.",
